---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../../../components/Callout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="TOTP (2FA)">
  <h1>TOTP &mdash; Time-Based One-Time Passwords</h1>
  <p>TOTP is the second-factor option for users who don't have a passkey. Identity issues an RFC-6238 secret, displays a QR code for the authenticator app, and verifies six-digit codes on every login.</p>

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Var</th><th>Default</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GATEWAY_TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code></td><td>(dev fallback)</td><td>32 bytes, base64. AES-GCM-encrypts every TOTP secret at rest. Required in prod.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GATEWAY_TOTP_ISSUER</code></td><td><code>Glassa Work</code></td><td>Name shown in the user's authenticator app entry.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GATEWAY_LOGIN_CHALLENGE_EXPIRY_SECONDS</code></td><td><code>300</code></td><td>How long after password success the user has to submit a TOTP code.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <Callout type="warning" title="TOTP secrets are encrypted at rest">
    The secret bytes stored on the <code>TOTPSecret</code> node (type_id 7) are AES-GCM-encrypted with the 32-byte key from <code>GATEWAY_TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>. Lose that key and every enrolled user has to re-enroll.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Enrollment</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash"># 1. Begin enrollment
curl -s -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/BeginTotpSetup \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{}'</code></pre>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-json">{
  "secret": "JBSWY3DPEHPK3PXP",
  "qrCodeUri": "otpauth://totp/Glassa%20Work:alice@example.com?secret=JBSWY3DPEHPK3PXP&issuer=Glassa%20Work",
  "recoveryCodes": [
    "a1b2-c3d4-e5f6",
    "g7h8-i9j0-k1l2",
    "..."
  ]
}</code></pre>
  <p>Show the QR code to the user. The 10 recovery codes are shown <em>once</em>; each is single-use and can substitute for a TOTP code at <code>VerifyTotp</code> time.</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash"># 2. User enters their first code from the authenticator
curl -s -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/VerifyTotpSetup \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"code":"123456"}'
# &rarr; { verified: true } and the user's totp_required flag is now true</code></pre>
  <p>Audit event: <code>totp_enabled</code>.</p>

  <h2>Login with TOTP</h2>
  <p>Password login for a TOTP-enabled user returns no tokens; instead it returns a login challenge:</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-json">{
  "user": { "id": "user_...", "totpRequired": true },
  "totpRequired": true,
  "loginChallengeId": "lc_..."
}</code></pre>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash"># Submit the TOTP code (or a recovery code)
curl -s -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/VerifyTotp \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "login_challenge_id": "lc_...",
    "code": "123456"
  }'
# &rarr; { user, accessToken, refreshToken, expiresIn }</code></pre>
  <p>The challenge is single-use; consuming it deletes the node atomically. Audit event: <code>totp_verified</code>.</p>

  <h2>Recovery codes</h2>
  <p>Stored as bcrypt hashes alongside the TOTP secret. Submitting a recovery code to <code>VerifyTotp</code> checks the hash list, marks the code as consumed, and issues tokens. To rotate the codes:</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/RegenerateRecoveryCodes \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"password":"Sup3rStrong!Pass"}'
# &rarr; { recoveryCodes: ["...new 10 codes..."] }</code></pre>
  <p>Password confirmation is required so a stolen short-lived access token can't silently rotate the codes.</p>

  <h2>Disable TOTP</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/DisableTotp \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"password":"Sup3rStrong!Pass"}'</code></pre>
  <p>Deletes the <code>TOTPSecret</code> node and clears <code>totp_required</code> on the user. Audit event: <code>totp_disabled</code>.</p>

  <h2>Algorithm details</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>RFC 6238 TOTP, 30-second step, 6-digit code, SHA-1.</li>
    <li>One-step skew tolerance (accepts the previous and next window) to handle clock drift.</li>
    <li>Verification uses constant-time comparison (<code>subtle.ConstantTimeCompare</code>).</li>
    <li>Re-using the same code within the same 30-second window is rejected to prevent replay.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
